WHY
Requested after the track was first closed: the divider blended into the rows it
separated, because bg-background is the same surface the rest of the table sits
on. The warm paper token gives it its own band. Recorded as its own phase rather
than folded into a completed one.

WHY THIS TOKEN IS SAFE TO REUSE
The landing palette ADDS tokens rather than redefining any dashboard surface, so
referencing one cannot alter anything else. There is precedent: the login and
signup left column already uses this colour. Critically, --landing-warm carries a
purpose-built dark value (oklch(0.212 0.016 70)) alongside its light one
(oklch(0.935 0.014 84.6), the prototype's #eee9df), so the divider does not need
a dark-mode branch of its own.

The band reads consistently in both themes because the token sits just BELOW the
page ground in light and just ABOVE it in dark — the same relationship inversion
the landing palette already uses for its own bands.

